Prince of Persia (apps/pop)

Engine (engine/)
  SDLPoP 1.23, by Dávid Nagy, Falcury and contributors: an open-source port
  of Prince of Persia for DOS, from a disassembly of the original.
  License: GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (engine/COPYING).
  Source: https://github.com/NagyD/SDLPoP, release v1.23, with frunk.store's
  changes for the browser in engine/sdlpop-web.patch (also
  tools/pop/sdlpop-web.patch in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store,
  whose tools/build-pop.mjs builds it). The patched source the build came
  from is engine/sdlpop-1.23-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: the game's waits hand the page its turn (emscripten_sleep
  with JSPI), so its own loops run as they are inside main(); SDL's
  controller support is off, since the page reads the controller itself
  (the car lists each controller twice) and sends keys; the action key
  (Shift) also picks in the pause menu; and a frame counter for the page.
  tools/pop/SDLPoP.ini sets the starting options (pause menu on, no
  splash, the original 4:3 picture, quick saves, the fixes and enhancements
  on); the player's own settings go to SDLPoP.cfg next to the saves.
  SDLPoP includes opl3.c (Nuked OPL3, by Alexey Khokholov, LGPL 2.1 or
  later) and stb_vorbis.c (by Sean Barrett, public domain / MIT); see the
  source.

Game data (engine/prince.data, preloaded at /pop/data)
  The graphics, levels, sounds and music of Prince of Persia (1989), by
  Jordan Mechner, published by Brøderbund, now owned by Ubisoft, as the
  SDLPoP repository ships them (its data folder). They are not covered by
  SDLPoP's license. frunk.store is not affiliated with or endorsed by
